  "name": "Question 11",
  "problem": "Calculate the determinant of the matrix\n$Z=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3 & 8\\end{aligned}]$",
  "worked_solution": "We use the cofactor expansion along the first row:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(Z) & ={z}_{11}{C}_{11}+{z}_{12}{C}_{12}+{z}_{13}{C}_{13}+{z}_{14}{C}_{14} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {C}_{11}+0\\cdot {C}_{12}+0\\cdot {C}_{13}+0\\cdot {C}_{14} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{C}_{11} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} & \u2217 & \u2217 & \u2217 \\\\ \u2217 & 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ \u2217 & 5 & 3 & 2 \\\\ \u2217 & 2 & 3 & 8\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(-1)^{1+1}|\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 8\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 8\\end{aligned}|-(-2)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 8\\end{aligned}|+0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}5 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}|) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(0+2(5\\cdot 8-2\\cdot 2)+0) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 72 \\\\  & =36\\end{aligned}\n$$",
